{
 "_comment": "tiny-chat MoR block, Stage 0 (experiments/tiny_chat_2026-10/PREREGISTRATION.md amendment 4, A4.4): the CUDA gate (every device leg of tools/colab_cuda_validate.sh, test_mor's included), a 300-step probe per cell (20m_MoR3, 20m_MC2, 20m_MC3), then screens at [0.00025, 0.0005, 0.001, 0.002] x 1500 steps, seed 101, on the 35% mix. MoR3 is causal token-choice Mixture-of-Recursions (arch.custom.recursion schedule mor: {'route': 'token_choice', 'gate': 'score', 'balance': 0.1, 'z_loss': 0.001, 'kv_rows': 'active'}); MC2 and MC3 fixed recursion at the same stored layers. One GPU job at a time. The gate needs the floor pilot's PASS; probes and screens need the CUDA gate passed on their VM. Estimated 5.5 L4 VM-hours (20m_L4's probe scaled by FLOPs per token, MoR3 at its largest depth x 1.2, until the block's probes come home). A4.7: this Stage 0 runs on Jonathan's go; the nine runs after the probes and his confirmation. Afterwards, at home: copy ART/cuda_gate/cuda_gate.json to experiments/tiny_chat_2026-10/recursion/cuda_gate_mor.json and the probe folders to experiments/tiny_chat_2026-10/stage0/mor/, then python tools/colab_chat/tiny_chat_run.py choose_rec --art ART --out experiments/tiny_chat_2026-10/stage0/lr_choice_mor.json, commit, rerun make_jobs.py. Upload vocab_llama3_bpe.gguf with the runner's --upload. Dialogue levels [0, 17, 35, 70]% (copies), E1 at 35% (design.json final).",
 "max_parallel": 1,
